201	However, on a collection page the widget is typically not useful (no single product context). Two approaches:
202	
203	**Recommended (V1):** Only pass `product.id` on product pages. Collection-based rules are resolved server-side by looking up the product's collections. The `data-collection-id` attribute is a bonus for future use but not required for rule matching.
204	
205	**Why:** A customer checks delivery for a specific product. Even if the rule targets a collection, the API resolves it by checking if the product belongs to that collection. The collection page context is secondary.
206	
207	### Widget on Non-Product Pages
208	
209	On pages without product context (homepage, custom pages), the widget sends no `product` param. The API returns only general rules (`targetType = "all"`). This is correct behavior.
210	
211	---
212	
213	## 4. ZIP Check API Changes
214	
215	### New Matching Priority (4-tier)
216	
217	```
218	1. Product-specific rules (targetType = "products", productIds contains this product)
219	2. Collection-specific rules (targetType = "collections", product belongs to collection)
220	3. Zone-based general rules (targetType = "all", zone or zipCodes match)
221	4. Default general rules (targetType = "all", no zone filter)
222	```
223	
224	Within each tier, rules are still sorted by `priority ASC` (lower = higher priority).
225	
226	### Updated API Signature
227	
228	```
229	GET /api/zip-check?shop=X&zip=Y&product=Z
230	```
231	
232	- `product` (optional): numeric Shopify product ID
233	- `collection` (optional): numeric Shopify collection ID (fallback context, lower priority than product)
234	
235	### Implementation Logic
236	
237	```typescript
238	async function handleZipCheck(shop: string, zip: string, productId?: string) {
239	  // ... existing zip record lookup unchanged ...
240	  
241	  // Fetch all active rules for this shop
242	  const activeRules = await db.deliveryRule.findMany({
243	    where: { shop, isActive: true },
244	    orderBy: { priority: "asc" },
245	  });
246	  
247	  let matchedRule = null;
248	  
249	  if (productId) {
250	    // PASS 1: Product-specific rules
251	    for (const rule of activeRules) {
252	      if (rule.targetType === "products" && rule.productIds) {
253	        const ids = rule.productIds.split(",").map(id => id.trim());
254	        if (ids.includes(productId)) {
255	          if (matchesZipOrZone(rule, normalizedZip, zipZone)) {
256	            matchedRule = rule;
257	            break;
258	          }
259	        }
260	      }
261	    }
262	    
263	    // PASS 2: Collection-specific rules
264	    if (!matchedRule) {
265	      const productCollections = await getProductCollections(shop, productId);
266	      for (const rule of activeRules) {
267	        if (rule.targetType === "collections" && rule.collectionIds) {
268	          const ruleCollectionIds = rule.collectionIds.split(",").map(id => id.trim());
269	          if (ruleCollectionIds.some(cid => productCollections.includes(cid))) {
270	            if (matchesZipOrZone(rule, normalizedZip, zipZone)) {
271	              matchedRule = rule;
272	              break;
273	            }
274	          }
275	        }
276	      }
277	    }
278	  }
279	  
280	  // PASS 3: Explicit zip match on general rules (existing logic)
281	  if (!matchedRule) {
282	    for (const rule of activeRules) {
283	      if (rule.targetType === "all" && rule.zipCodes) {
284	        const zips = rule.zipCodes.split(",").map(z => z.trim().toUpperCase());
285	        if (zips.includes(normalizedZip)) {
286	          matchedRule = rule;
287	          break;
288	        }
289	      }
290	    }
291	  }
292	  
293	  // PASS 4: Zone match on general rules (existing logic)
294	  if (!matchedRule && zipZone) {
295	    for (const rule of activeRules) {
296	      if (rule.targetType === "all" && rule.zone === zipZone && !rule.zipCodes?.trim()) {
297	        matchedRule = rule;
298	        break;
299	      }
300	    }
301	  }
302	  
303	  // ... rest of response construction unchanged ...
304	}
305	```
306	
307	### Helper: `matchesZipOrZone`
308	
309	Product/collection rules still need to be constrained by geography. A rule targeting "Product X in Zone A" should not match if the customer's ZIP is in Zone B.
310	
311	```typescript
312	function matchesZipOrZone(
313	  rule: DeliveryRule, 
314	  normalizedZip: string, 
315	  zipZone: string | null
316	): boolean {
317	  // If rule has explicit zip codes, check those
318	  if (rule.zipCodes?.trim()) {
319	    const zips = rule.zipCodes.split(",").map(z => z.trim().toUpperCase());
320	    return zips.includes(normalizedZip);
321	  }
322	  // If rule has a zone, check zone match
323	  if (rule.zone) {
324	    return rule.zone === zipZone;
325	  }
326	  // No geographic constraint = matches all zips
327	  return true;
328	}
329	```
330	
331	**Key design decision:** Product/collection rules can optionally be combined with zone/zip constraints. This lets merchants create rules like "Product X in Manhattan = $5 fee" vs "Product X in Brooklyn = $8 fee". If no zone/zip is specified on a product rule, it applies everywhere.
332	
333	### Collection Membership Lookup
334	
335	```typescript
336	async function getProductCollections(
337	  shop: string, 
338	  productId: string
339	): Promise<string[]> {
340	  // Check cache first (TTL: 6 hours)
341	  const sixHoursAgo = new Date(Date.now() - 6 * 60 * 60 * 1000);
342	  const cached = await db.productCollectionCache.findMany({
343	    where: {
344	      shop,
345	      productId,
346	      cachedAt: { gt: sixHoursAgo },
347	    },
348	    select: { collectionId: true },
349	  });
350	  
351	  if (cached.length > 0) {
352	    return cached.map(c => c.collectionId);
353	  }
354	  
355	  // Cache miss: fetch from Shopify API
356	  try {
357	    const collectionIds = await fetchProductCollectionsFromShopify(shop, productId);
358	    
359	    // Store in cache (upsert to handle race conditions)
360	    await Promise.all(
361	      collectionIds.map(collectionId =>
362	        db.productCollectionCache.upsert({
363	          where: {
364	            shop_productId_collectionId: { shop, productId, collectionId },
365	          },
366	          create: { shop, productId, collectionId },
367	          update: { cachedAt: new Date() },
368	        })
369	      )
370	    );
371	    
372	    // Clean up old entries for this product (they may have been removed from collections)
373	    await db.productCollectionCache.deleteMany({
374	      where: {
375	        shop,
376	        productId,
377	        cachedAt: { lt: sixHoursAgo },
378	      },
379	    });
380	    
381	    return collectionIds;
382	  } catch (error) {
383	    console.error("[zip-check] Failed to fetch collections for product", productId, error);
384	    // On API failure, return empty -- fall through to general rules
385	    return [];
386	  }
387	}
388	```
